/-!
# Lifting anti-fixed elements along the refined `2`-central filtration of a free group

`Work.SSGRoute.freeGroup_refinedTerm_lifting`: if `σ` is a fixed-point-free involution of `X`,
`F = FreeGroup X`, `Φ = FreeGroup.freeGroupCongr σ` and `P = refinedTerm 2 F i j` is any term of
Schmidt–Wingberg's refined `2`-central filtration, then

  `(Φ w) * w ∈ P → ∃ n ∈ P, (Φ (w * n)) * (w * n) = 1`,

i.e. every anti-fixed element of `F ⧸ P` has an anti-fixed lift to `F`.

## Proof structure

* The lifting statement for `N` is *equivalent* to the norm statement (`LiftingAux.lifting_of_target`):
  every `Φ`-anti-fixed element of `F ⧸ N` is a norm `x = (Φ̄ r)⁻¹ * r`.
* Norm statements are proved by *descending induction on `k`* for all `N ⊇ P_k`
  (`LiftingAux.normStatement_of_pCentralSeries_le`), the descent step being
  `Work.SSGRoute.central_descent_antifixed_weak` with central subgroup the image of `P_k`.
  The only input of the descent is the `k`-th *graded step* `LiftingAux.GradedStep`
  (`LiftingAux.normStatement_of_pCentralSeries_le` takes it as its hypothesis).
## WARNING: the `LayerGen` route of earlier sessions is REFUTED

Earlier sessions reduced the file to `∀ k ≥ 1, LiftingAux.LayerGen k` and this was recorded here as
"the single remaining input".  **That statement is false**, so the reduction, while formally valid
(`LiftingAux.gradedStep_of_layerGen` is a true implication from a false hypothesis), is useless:

* `LayerGen k` says that on the layer `V = P_{k-1}/P_k` (`P_n = Work.Shrinking.pCentralSeries 2 F n`)
  the `Φ̄`-fixed part is generated by the orbit sums `Φ̄ a * a` of the layer together with the norms
  `(Φ̄ r)⁻¹ * r` of witnesses `r` in the image of `P_{k-2}` (one level down).
* For `k ≥ 4` that witness family is too small.  At `X = Fin 2`, `σ =` the swap, `k = 4`,
  `N = P_4`, the fixed part of `P_3/P_4` has `𝔽₂`-dimension `5`, whereas the generation span has
  dimension `4` (defect `m²` at rank `2m`); the same happens at `k = 6`.  See
  `Submission/Work/SSGRoute/NOTE_layerGenMinimal5_verified.md` §2 (exact Magnus computations) and
  `Submission/Work/SSGRoute/layerGenMinimalFive.lean`,
  `Submission/Work/SSGRoute/freeGroup_refinedTerm_lifting_fin_zmodTwo.lean` (both record the
